    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="1016" n="1002" xml:id="pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Registration/7–1844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-28T14:00:00-04:00">July 28, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1010. 1. Department is gratified to learn from your 1235, July 18, 10 a.m., that
                    Minister of Economic Affairs has agreed to extend period of registration until
                    the end of this year.</p>
                <p>2. With reference to Embassy’s request for information in regard to our
                    registration requirements in the United States for foreign corporations and the
                    legal requirements in other countries, National Foreign Trade Council in a
                    further memorandum regarding Chinese registration touches on the subject of
                    requirements in this country and cites pertinent provisions of Delaware
                    corporation law. The memorandum in question has been forwarded to you<anchor
                        n="31" xml:id="d742-f1"/> and Department will endeavor to forward other
                    pertinent information on this subject in the near future.</p>
                <p>3. With reference to your suggestion that during visit of Dr. Kung in the United
                    States the dissatisfaction of American interests with Chinese laws and
                    regulations should be brought to his attention, Department understands that the
                    National Foreign Trade Council and the China–America Council of Commerce and
                    Industry propose to bring this problem and related problems to Dr. Kung’s
                    attention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
